course: dictionary
lesson: 10625
title: Two meanings of unfit
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Unfit can describe a person's body, or whether a thing is good enough for a job. Context tells you which meaning to use. «Asthma is not catching and not a sign of being unfit» is about people and sport, so here unfit means not strong or healthy.
explain: To check, swap your meaning into the sentence. If unfit means not healthy, «a sign of being not healthy» makes sense in the sentence. If it meant not suitable, the sentence would not make sense. The clue «with good control people with asthma can do every sport» also points to fitness in the body.
explain: Unfit is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a person, a shed or some water. Often a word that follows it tells you the meaning: «unfit to drink» means not safe to drink, and «unfit for use» means it cannot do its job.
fact: Unfit means not healthy or strong in the body, usually because of too little exercise.
fact: Unfit also means not good enough or not suitable for something, such as water unfit to drink.
fact: «Unfit for purpose» means a thing does not do the job it was made for.
fact: «Asthma is not catching and not a sign of being unfit»: having asthma does not mean a person is unfit.
fact: The forms more unfit and unfittest are rare, so you will mostly see plain unfit.
exercise: Coach says, «Sam is unfit after weeks off training.» What does unfit mean here? | Lost in the park | *Not strong or healthy, from too little exercise | Ready to run a race | Very loud and cheerful
exercise: «The water was unfit to drink, so we boiled it first.» What does unfit mean? | *Not safe or suitable to drink | Very tasty | Cold and clear | Full of fish
exercise: What does «unfit for use» mean? | It is used every day | It is brand new | It is very big | *It does not do its job
test: «Asthma is not catching and not a sign of being unfit.» What does unfit mean in this sentence? | Not suitable for a job | *Not strong or healthy in the body | Very happy after a good meal | Sleepy from the cold
test: Which sentence uses unfit to mean not good enough or not suitable? | Mia was unfit after her long holiday in bed | *The milk had gone bad and was unfit to drink | Ben is unfit, so he gets puffed out on the stairs | Our team is unfit and needs more training
exam: Jayden says unfit means ugly. What does it really mean? | *Not healthy or strong, or not suitable | Ugly to look at | Very fast in a race | Happy with food
